# 🔥 Golden Interview Takeaway

> **Replication aur Partitioning dono scale karte hain, lekin alag problems solve karte hain.**  
> **Replication = Same data ki multiple copies (Availability + Fault Tolerance).**  
> **Partitioning (Sharding) = Data ko divide karna (Horizontal Scalability).**

> **Range Partitioning** range queries ke liye best hai lekin **Hot Spots** create kar sakta hai.  
> **Hash Partitioning** load evenly distribute karta hai lekin efficient range queries lose ho jaati hain.  

> **Local Secondary Index** writes ko fast banata hai, jabki **Global Secondary Index** reads ko fast banata hai, lekin uske liye distributed transactions aur synchronization ka overhead aata hai.